  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "description": "The importer declares an enum of the same name as the library's (lib.esm) with DIFFERENT values (`g_per_hp_hr` 7 and `g_per_gallon` 9, where the library says 1 and 2). Enums are file-local (esm-spec §9.3): the library's own `enum` op keeps 1 and the library's own call `gallon_code` keeps 2, while every symbol the IMPORTER spells resolves against the importer's block: its own `enum` ops, one it binds into a template parameter, a symbol it binds into `activity_code`, and one it binds through `code_via`'s forwarded parameter.",
    "name": "library_enum_importer_redeclares"
  },
